        "veste Indiana"@pt ;
    skos:definition "Men's loose-skirted wraps worn informally from the 17th to early 19th century; so called from their resemblance to similar garments worn by Banyans, a caste of Hindu merchants. Also refers to women's garments based on the men's banyan (AAT)"@en ;
