euf:10135 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "indianische Umhängetasche"@de,
        "φισεκλίκι"@el,
        "sac bandoulière"@fr,
        "mala a tiracolo / cinturão de cartucheira"@pt ;
    skos:definition "General purpose bags carried by North American Indians with attached shoulder straps worn over the shoulder and across the breast. Usually made of wool, muslin, or buckskin and heavily decorated with beadwork, quillwork, or embroidery. For shoulder belts worn across the breast from which wallets, small bags, or pockets often containing ammunition are sometimes suspended, use bandoliers. (AAT)"@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:europeana-fashion ;
