euf:10358 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Any material that is produced or created by humans through various processes, rather than occurring naturally in its current form. These materials are intentionally designed, modified, or synthesized to possess specific properties and characteristics that make them suitable for various applications. Manmade materials can range from those that involve minimal processing of natural resources ( artificial material ) to those that are entirely synthesized from basic chemical components ( synthetic material )."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:europeana-fashion ;
    skos:prefLabel "Man Gemacht Material"@de,
        "τεχνητό υλικό"@el,
        "manmade material"@en,
        "material hecho por el hombre"@es,
        "matériaux synthétiques"@fr,
        "חומר מעשה ידי אדם"@he,
