euf:10364 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Synthetic material refers to materials that are entirely human-made and are not found in nature. These materials are created by chemically synthesizing various compounds to form new substances with specific properties. Synthetic materials are often designed to have desirable characteristics such as strength, durability, and specific performance qualities."@en ;
