        "installatie"@nl,
        "instalacija"@sr,
        "installation"@sv .

euf:10667 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Kostümzeichnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "After reading the script the costume designer may develop ideas digitally or on paper. If the designer is too busy on the production or the sketch requires a slick finish (such as a super-hero) they may work with a costume illustrator. Many designers choose to use mood boards, collages of inspiration as communication tools. Whether or not sketches are created is ultimately irrelevant. The characters on screen define the “art of costume” (UCLA)"@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:europeana-fashion ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kostümskizze (Kostümdesign)"@de,
        "σκίτσο ενδύματος (σχέδιο ενδύματος)"@el,
        "costume sketch (costume design)"@en,
        "figurín"@es,
        "croquis de mode"@fr,
        "סקיצה תחפושת"@he,
        "figurino di moda"@it,
        "kostuumschets (kostuumontwerp)"@nl,
        "skica za kostim"@sr,
        "dräktskiss"@sv .

euf:10668 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Anschlussdokumentationsbuch (Film)"@de,
        "Buch zur Dokumentation der Dreharbeiten (Film)"@de,
        "Continuity Script"@de ;
    skos:definition "The collected notes kept by the script supervisor of each and every shot of every scene in the film. Films are not shot in chronological order. Continuity is a vital tool in post-production for the film editor who will assemble these thousands of pieces of footage (UCLA)"@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:europeana-fashion ;
    skos:prefLabel "Continuity Book"@de,
        "continuity book"@el,
        "continuity book"@en,
        "notas del guionista"@es,
        "script"@fr,
        "ספר מעקב"@he,
        "continuïteitsrapport"@nl,
        "knjiga kontinuiteta"@sr,
        "handledning"@sv .

euf:10669 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Buch zur Dokumentation der Kostüme (Film/ Theater)"@de,
        "Kostümbibel (Film/ Theater)"@de,
        "skice kostima"@sr ;
    skos:definition "A volume of collected research including photographs, contemporary and historic text, sketches, hair and makeup notes, inspiration, memoirs (family albums), fabric and color fabric samples (swatches)swatches. It may be shared with the director, production designer, the costume crew, actors and the hair and makeup artists. Some designers create websites as with research online, available to all collaborators and actors as needed. (UCLA)"@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:europeana-fashion ;
    skos:prefLabel "Costume Bible"@de,
        "βίβλος ενδύματος"@el,
        "costume bible"@en,
        "dossier"@es,
        "bible du costume (film)"@fr,
        "ספר התלבושות"@he,
        "raccolta delle informazioni sui costumi di una produzione"@it,
        "kostuumbijbel (filmindustrie)"@nl,
        "knjiga kostima"@sr,
        "kostymundelar (film/teater)"@sv .

