    skos:definition "Warp pile weave, typically silk, with a short, soft dense pile produced by a supplementary warp that is raised in loops above the surface of the textile through the introduction of rods during the weaving; the loops may be cut or left uncut (AAT)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:europeana-fashion ;
