    skos:definition "The Talosel is a material invented around 1960 by the artist Line Vautrin consisting of layers of resin superimposed, scraped, scarified and worked with fire with the inclusion of various materials such as mirror shards. The name is made of borrowings from the designation of the material, acétate de cellulose élaboré (proantic.com)."@en ;
