        "purperharthout"@nl,
        "štir"@sr ;
    skos:definition "Strong, elastic purplish wood derived from several species of the genus Peltogyne. The heartwood is brown when freshly cut becoming deep purple upon exposure to air, eventually turning to a dark brown with sharply demarcated off-white sapwood. Has a fine, uniform texture and grain that is straight or slightly roey. The durable, shock-resistant wood is sometimes used for carving and for vehicle construction. Also used widely in furniture-making, marquetry, veneers, flooring, etc. (AAT)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:europeana-fashion ;
    skos:prefLabel "Amarant"@de,
