euf:11165 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Paper, typically handmade, manufactured by casting the pulp onto a woven screen made from wire mesh or fabric. When examined in transmitted light, wove paper shows a characteristic weave impression from the screen pattern. It is distinguished from laid paper, which shows a pattern of thick and thin transucent lines that have been transmitted from a wire screen used in manufacture (AAT)."@en ;
