euf:11338 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Objects with a highly polished surface, designed to reflect images clearly. The surface is typically smooth, flat, or sometimes slightly curved, made of polished metal in ancient and medieval times, but later usually of glass with a reflective coating on one side (AAT)."@en ;
