    skos:prefLabel "light bluish green"@en .

aat:300128688 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Negatives having gelatin as the binder, holding silver as the final image material; may be on glass (\"gelatin dry plate negatives\") or on film."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gelatin silver negatives"@en .

aat:300128695 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Refers to photographic prints having gelatin as the binder, holding silver as the final image material; always black-and-white, though they may be toned to a monochrome hue."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gelatin silver prints"@en .

aat:300128739 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Refers to the technique of detecting underground water, minerals, treasure, archaeological remains, and even dead bodies by feeling the motion of a divining rod. A Y-shaped twig is the traditional divining rod, its two prongs twisting or dipping in the hand of the dowser to indicate the nearby presence of the material sought; alternatively metal rods are held parallel a few inches apart and swing across each other. The nature of the stimuli causing these reactions is unexplained, but most dowsers deny that it is a matter of divination."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dowsing"@en .

aat:300129031 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Large, subterranean, naturally formed chambers, with entrances from the surface."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "caverns"@en .

