aat:300446228 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a type of āliṅga band or fillet, usually carved, such as at the base of a wall or other element."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "āliṅga-paṭṭikā"@en .

aat:300446229 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an almshouse."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "puṇyaśālā"@en .

aat:300446230 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, alpanāsī, nāsī (minor dormer)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kṣudranāsī"@en .

aat:300446231 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an altar; group of wall mouldings (above the adhisthana); plank-moulding below the grīvā-śikhara."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "vēdī"@en .

aat:300446232 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art or architecture, a amorous couple."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "rati-nāyaka"@en .

aat:300446233 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Indian ancient and medieval dance-form, perhaps of foreign (Śaka?) origin."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "hallīśaka"@en .

aat:300446235 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an angular subdivision of the bhadra."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "bhadra-phālanā"@en .

aat:300446236 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a angular subdivision of the karṇa."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "karṇa-phālanā"@en .

aat:300446237 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a antefix above the roof of the kapilī; forward-drawn fronton or antefix of a vimāna-superstructure (Karṇāṭan, North Indian) occurring above the kapilī-walls; antefix at the front of the superstructure."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "śukanāsikā"@en .

aat:300446246 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Hindu art, anthropomorphic or personified depictions of a divine weapon, often a partial incarnation of their divine owner. The noun is masculine or feminine, depending upon the gender of the word for the weapon in Sanskrit."@en ;
