    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a cubical pillar-part."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "caduram"@en .

aat:300446437 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a curvature based on a radius of four-unit measures."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "caturguṇa-sūtra"@en .

aat:300446438 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a curvature of śikhara."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "rēkhā"@en .

aat:300446439 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a curvature of three segments in vēṇukōśa."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "trikhaṇḍā rēkhā"@en .

aat:300446440 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a curved and ribbed eave or awning; kūṭacchādya."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "khuracchādya"@en .

aat:300446441 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a curvilinear śikhara with four marked levels."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "caturkhaṇḍa rēkhā"@en .

aat:300446442 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a cusped and coffered ceiling with a central lambana-pendentive."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "sabhāmandāraka"@en .

aat:300446443 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a cusped and downward projecting miniature pendentive or recessed cusp (ceiling ornament), whose series is often arranged around the central lambana."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "lūmā"@en .

aat:300446444 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a cyma-eave/cornice."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kapōtālī"@en .

aat:300446445 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Indian architecture, a cyma-eave/cornice; flexured minor cornice of a base/entablature."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kapōtapālikā"@en .

aat:300446446 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, cyma-fillet."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmavājana"@en .

aat:300446447 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a cyma-recta at base of adhiṣṭhāna."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmapādukā"@en .

aat:300446448 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a dais; platform; prastara; adhiṣṭhāna-type; adhiṣṭhāna type without kumuda."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mañca"@en .

aat:300446449 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a dais-like moulding supporting figure-bearing niches on the wall frieze; pedestal-like moulding in the lower section of a temple-wall."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mañcikā"@en .

aat:300446450 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a temple theatre for dance or music, used for staging Koothu, Nangiar koothu and Koodiyattam, which are ancient ritualistic art forms. The structures are said to be constructed according to the guidelines given in the Nātyasāstra of Bharata Muni; hall for theatre performances (kūdiyāṭṭam)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kūttambalams"@en .

aat:300446451 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a dancing Śiva figure set in śukanāsa’s great nāsī, or occurring in the central box of a compartmental ceiling; as pantheonic image on the temple walls."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "naṭēśa"@en .

aat:300446452 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a decorative band bearing cakvā-birds in file."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "cakravākamālā"@en .

aat:300446453 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a decorative band showing leafy vine motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "parṇamālāpaṭṭī"@en .

aat:300446454 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a decorative door-band; door-jamb."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "śākhā"@en .

aat:300446455 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a decorative half-dormer-like form."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "ardhanāsī"@en .

aat:300446456 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Complex spirelet with several miniature aṇḍaka-spirelets."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "karma"@en .

aat:300446458 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a demigod figure, placed on top of the śikhara (Orissa)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dēvalacāraṇi"@en .

aat:300446459 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a demi-goddess placed at the bhadra point of skandha of the śikhara (Oriyā); also beki-Bhairava (male: Oriyā)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "deulcāraṇī"@en .

aat:300446460 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a depressed, curved recess in doorframe; or as water-conduit; plain recess."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "khalva"@en .

aat:300446461 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art and architecture, a design of intertwined serpents."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "nāgapāśa"@en .

aat:300446462 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, detached maṇḍapas, halls for paying obeisance (colloquial Kēraḷa term). Integral parts of the temple architecture, places where the priests and Brahmins sit to recite hymns."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "namaskāra-maṇḍapas"@en .

aat:300446464 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a diamond hand (decorative pattern)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "vajrabandha"@en .

aat:300446465 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A diminutive form of nāsī."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "nāsikā"@en .

aat:300446466 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Diminutive of candraśālā; induśālikā; decorative dormer motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "candraśālikā"@en .

aat:300446467 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a diminutive of maṇḍapa; temple-type with pillared walls and usually Muṇḍamāla (flat or without superstructure)/with only a \"vēdī\" superstructure; pandal; small pillared structure; pillared pavilion; small pavilion."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "maṇḍapikā"@en .

aat:300446468 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a diminutive of ratnapaṭṭa; band of diamond pattern; maṇipaṭṭa, maṇipaṭṭikā; minor jewel-band ."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "ratnapaṭṭī"@en .

aat:300446469 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a dining hall."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "ūṭṭupura"@en .

aat:300446471 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a distinctively detailed vertical foliage pattern (decorative motif); coconut tree."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "śrīvṛkṣa"@en .

aat:300446472 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a distribution of adorning deities; deities as adornment on the temple and hall walls."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dēvālaṁkāra"@en .

aat:300446473 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, ornamentation consisting of divine figures, usually on an exterior wall."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "alaṁkāra-dēvatā"@en .

aat:300446474 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In various Eastern religions, a type of incarnation of a deity."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "avatāra"@en .

aat:300446475 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a division of doorframe into jambs; vertical facia-division of a doorframe."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "śākhā-vibhakti"@en .

aat:300446476 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a door."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dvāra"@en .

aat:300446477 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a door with three jambs."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "triśākhadvāra"@en .

aat:300446478 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a doorframe."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dvārabandha"@en .

aat:300446479 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a doorframe having four śākhās (jambs)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "catuḥśākha"@en .

aat:300446480 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a doorframe having two śākhās/ jambs; two-jambed doorframe."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dviśākha"@en .

aat:300446481 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a doorframe with a single decorative door-jamb/band."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "ēkaśākhā"@en .

aat:300446482 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a doorframe with jamb-divisions."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "śākhā-yukta"@en .

aat:300446483 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a doorframe with seven jambs; with seven śākhās."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "saptaśākhā"@en .

aat:300446484 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a door-guardian."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dvārapālas"@en .

aat:300446485 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a door-jamb bearing pramathas or amorini figures."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "pramathaśākhā"@en .

aat:300446486 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a door-jamb bearing vidyādharas (often with vidyādharīs or consorts in medieval Karṇāṭan temples)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "vidyādharaśākhā"@en .

aat:300446487 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a door-jamb carved with goblins/bhūtas."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "bhūtaśākhā"@en .

aat:300446488 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, doorjambs ornamented with celestial musicians; śākhā ornamented with gandharvas; door-jamb showing heavenly minstrels (placed in upward moving series)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gandharvaśākhā"@en .

aat:300446489 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, doorjambs ornamented with dwarf figures; śākhā ornamented with gaṇas; jamb showing gaṇas."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gaṇaśākhā"@en .

aat:300446490 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a door-jamb showing lotus-garland as decoration."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padma-mālā"@en .

aat:300446491 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, door-lintel; uttaraṅga."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "pataṅga"@en .

aat:300446492 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a doorsill; udumbara; threshold."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "bhuvaṅga"@en .

aat:300446493 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a dormer-window decorative motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "caitya-gavākṣa"@en .

aat:300446495 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a down-turned minor cyma molding."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "adhaḥcippikā"@en .

aat:300446496 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, drama-theatre."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "nāṭyaśālā"@en .

aat:300446497 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art or architecture, a dramatic figure-composition."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "pratirūpaka"@en .

aat:300446498 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Drāviḍa-śikhara, on the superstructure of a vimāna or over a Phāṁsanā."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "Drāviḍa ghaṇṭā"@en .

aat:300446499 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a dwarf atlantan figure."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kīcaka"@en .

aat:300446501 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A dynasty-name sometimes wrongly used as name of superstructure-type."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kadamba"@en .

aat:300446502 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a eagle; goose (decorative motif); Harpy (decorative motif)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "suparṇa"@en .

aat:300446503 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art, a representation of an earring, an earring motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "karṇakuṇḍala"@en .

aat:300446504 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an eave, cornice, or tier in the form of a stepped, pyramidal roof."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "phaṁsa-kapōta"@en .

aat:300446505 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an eave-cornice, or awning."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "chādya"@en .

aat:300446506 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an echinus; Types: pāli, padma, nāgadala."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "maṇḍi"@en .

aat:300446507 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, refers to a side; often joined in words, for example in as \"dvayasra\" or \"caturasra.\""@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "asra"@en .

aat:300446508 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian culture, literally \"Eight Auspicious Symbols,\" endemic to a number of Dharmic Traditions, which may vary slightly. Examples are in Sanatana Dharma, Jaina Dharma, Buddhadharma, and Sikha Dharma."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "aṣṭamaṅgala"@en .

aat:300446511 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Conjunction of the Sun, Moon, Earth, Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn. It was considered a sign of imminent disaster."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "aṣṭagraha"@en .

aat:300446513 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art and architecture, sub-shrines for eight subsidiary deities."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "aṣṭaparivāra"@en .

aat:300446514 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Hinduism, attendant deities, usually eight in number."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "vasus"@en .

aat:300446515 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, eight-jambed doorframe."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "aṣṭaśākhā"@en .

aat:300446516 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a type of ceiling in the shape of an eight-petalled lotus."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "aṣṭadala"@en .

aat:300446518 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "An elephant band motif in base."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gajapaṭṭī"@en .

aat:300446519 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an elephant band in base."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gajāvalī"@en .

aat:300446520 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an elephant eye; perforated screen (jāla) with holes, looking like geometricised \"elephant eye.\""@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "hastinētra"@en .

aat:300446521 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an elephant frieze."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gajamālā"@en .

aat:300446522 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Motif of an elephant head."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gajamukha"@en .

aat:300446523 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Refers to “elephant trunk” and represents one of the four Elirkai gestures, as defined according to texts dealing with śilpa (arts and crafts), known as śilpaśāstras. Comprised of hand gestures (hasta, mudrā or kai-amaiti), stances/poses (āsanas) and inflexions of the body (bhaṅgas). When the hand is stretched straight out, and the palm slopes downward from the wrist, with the fingers bent gracefully like tendrils on a creeper, this regal mudrā reminiscent of an elephant’s trunk, is called gaja-hasta."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gajahasta"@en .

aat:300446524 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an elephant’s palate; cusped ceiling-course; decorative motif of ceiling."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gajatālu"@en .

aat:300446525 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "An elephant's head (decorative motif)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gajamuṇḍa"@en .

aat:300446526 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an elephant-trunk; fluted design of praṇāla; water spout."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "śuṇḍu"@en .

aat:300446527 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, elliptical; elliptical temple-type."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "vṛttāyata"@en .

aat:300446528 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an elongated udgama (Eastern India)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "lambinī"@en .

aat:300446529 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an eminent Buddhist monastery."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mahāvihāra"@en .

aat:300446530 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, enclosing walls interspersed by parivāra shrines."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "parivārālaya-prākāra"@en .

aat:300446531 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a wall enclosing the garbha."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "āvaraṇa"@en .

aat:300446533 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an entrance-gate with śālā-śikhara."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dvāra-gōpura"@en .

aat:300446534 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an entrance-structure."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "paḍippura"@en .

aat:300446535 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an entry projection."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mukhabhadra"@en .

aat:300446537 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art or architecture, a erotic depiction; erotic act."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "ratikrīḍā"@en .

aat:300446538 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a projection of the eave."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "avalambana"@en .

aat:300446539 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, an eave-strut; cantilever of a faceted, lotus-stalk form; usually a faceted lotiformed cantilever."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mṛṇālikā"@en .

aat:300446540 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Pose in Indian art and culture where the legs are highly flexed."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "atibhaṅga"@en .

aat:300446541 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a fabulous figure in the form of dolphin with elephant-trunk; decorative figure, sometimes used for temple conduits (Kaliṅga); karimakara."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mātaṅga-nakra"@en .

aat:300446542 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art and architecture, a representation of the face of a divine female minstrel."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kinnarīvaktra"@en .

aat:300446543 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a facetted element."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dhārānvita"@en .

aat:300446544 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a facetted coping piece."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dhārānvita uṣṇīṣa"@en .

aat:300446545 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a depending ornament decorative motif; decorative central pendentive in larger ceiling; central pendent of a Sabhāmandāraka and Sabhā-padma-mandāraka ceilings."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "lambana"@en .

aat:300446546 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a false door applied on the central offset."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
