    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a kūṭa-niche; kūṭa and sālā together; niche having a kūṭa as its crowning member."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kūṭakōṣṭha"@en .

aat:300446767 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Motif representing Lakṣmī with a pair of elephants performing lustral ceremony; in architecture usually a tutelary image at the \"lalāṭa\" block of the doorframe."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "abhiṣēka-Lakṣmī"@en .

aat:300446769 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a large gavākṣa front of a vaulted, apsidal structure."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "lalaṭanāsikā"@en .

aat:300446771 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lamp post."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dīpastambha"@en .

aat:300446772 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A lamp-bearing maiden in Indian sculpture or architecture."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dīpalakṣmī"@en .

aat:300446773 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In North Indian architecture, a large cogged-wheel-shaped stone crowning element of the śikhara-spire."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "āmalasāraka"@en .

aat:300446774 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a large flanking or lateral gable-nāsīs of a bhadraśālā-aedicule; lateral nāsī."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kukṣināsī"@en .

aat:300446775 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a large gavākṣa dormer (South India); large nāsī; dormer at the cardinal and sometimes subcardinal points of the śikhara; cardinal nāsi; facial larger dormer of a śikhara-cupola; figuring also at the śukanāsa-front in Karṇāṭan vimānas."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mahānāsī"@en .

aat:300446776 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lateral nāsī-dormer."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "pārśvanāsī"@en .

aat:300446777 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lateral porch of a maṇḍapa/ hall."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "pārśvacatuṣkī"@en .

aat:300446778 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, lateral screens at the antarāla or vestibule’s entryway."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "antarāla-jālas"@en .

aat:300446779 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lathe-turned bed-stead like round-shafted pillar; Rudrakānta or Īśakānta (Karṇāṭan version); lathe-turned column with inverted pot member (of Karṇāṭa temples)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "Śrīkāra"@en .

aat:300446780 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a Latina-style temple having eight pointed karṇas or corners."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "aṣṭakarṇa-Latina"@en .

aat:300446781 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lattice of gavākṣa."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gavākṣajāla"@en .

aat:300446784 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a leaf of Xanthochymus pictonius L. (decorative motif)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "tamāla"@en .

aat:300446785 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a leaf of Xanthochymus pictonius L. (decorative motif)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "tamālapatra"@en .

aat:300446786 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, leaf or foliage motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "patra"@en .

aat:300446787 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art and architecture, a leafy scroll; vine, leaf, or floral-band motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "patralatā"@en .

aat:300446788 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a leaning damsel figure at the pillar-bracket."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "citraputrikā"@en .

aat:300446789 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a leaning half-spire of Śekharī superstructure; half-spire leaning against an upper uraḥmañjarī, also against the mūlamañjarī or central spire."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "uraḥmañjarī"@en .

aat:300446790 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A forest-creeper motif in Indian architecture."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "vanalatā"@en .

aat:300446791 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a liṅga-shaped shrine-type described in early śilpa texts."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "Liṅgākāra"@en .

aat:300446792 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lintel or architrave facia."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "uttara-paṭṭikā"@en .

aat:300446793 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lintel, beam; door-architrave or door-lintel; pataṅga."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "uttaraṅga"@en .

aat:300446794 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lion (decorative motif)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "siṁha"@en .

aat:300446795 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lion headed composite fabulous animal; gryphon; lion-vyāla motif; leonine vyāla-type."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "siṁhavyāla"@en .

aat:300446796 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Lion pouncing on elephant decorative motif; kari-kumbha-vidari."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gajākrānta-siṁha"@en .

aat:300446797 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lion-based column-type."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "siṁhapāda"@en .

aat:300446798 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lion-crest."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "siṁhaśikha"@en .

aat:300446799 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lion-crest."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "siṁhōtsēdha-śikhā"@en .

aat:300446800 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lion-monster; a tiger-vyāla."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "śārdūla"@en .

aat:300446801 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lion's head nāsī-top."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "siṁhavaktra"@en .

aat:300446802 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lion's head; lion’s mouth holding water-chute."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "siṁhamukha"@en .

aat:300446803 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lion-throne."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "siṁhāsana"@en .

aat:300446804 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, literally \"earth\", ground, tala, level; a floor or storey of a prāsāda; symbolic storey in Latina śikhara."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "bhūmi"@en .

aat:300446807 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a little pillar; pillarette."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "stambhikā"@en .

aat:300446808 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art and architecture, a long garland worn by Viṣṇu."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "vanamālā"@en .

aat:300446809 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a looped bell-garland."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kiṅkiṇīmālā"@en .

aat:300446810 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a loti-formed crowning member."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmakūṭa"@en .

aat:300446811 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, lotus foliage, lotus leaf; series of lotus petals carved on the external-most jamb."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmapatra"@en .

aat:300446812 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus frieze; string-course with half-lotuses in series."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmapaṭṭikā"@en .

aat:300446813 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus pedestal."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmapīṭha"@en .

aat:300446814 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus petal motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmadala"@en .

aat:300446815 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus umbrella; loti-formed cap above the āmalaka of a Bhūmija śikhara."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmacchatra"@en .

aat:300446816 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, lotus vine; lotus-creeper motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmalatā"@en .

aat:300446817 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus vine motif; padmalatā."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmavallī"@en .

aat:300446818 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus/floral bud conical decorative motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mukula"@en .

aat:300446819 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, lotus; inverted cyma-recta moulding with (or without) lotus-petal pattern as decoration; loti-formed mandi-type; lotus-shaped cupola-cap; lotus motif"@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padma"@en .

aat:300446820 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus-based column-type."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmapāda"@en .

aat:300446821 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus-bearing nidhi."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmanidhi"@en .

aat:300446822 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus-bud motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kuḍamala"@en .

aat:300446823 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus-capital."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmabharaṇa"@en .

aat:300446824 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, lotus-formed upāna (South India)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmōpāna"@en .

aat:300446825 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus-ornamented jamb; door-jamb, usually outermost, showing lotus petal-decoration; śākhā with pattern of lotus petals."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmaśākhā"@en .

aat:300446826 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus-petal edged minor cyma moulding."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmacippikā"@en .

aat:300446827 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lotus-web; chain of lotuses with each lotus set within a beaded semi-circle; festoons with hemicycles filled with half lotuses."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmajāla"@en .

aat:300446828 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lower ‘kampa or lower fillet of an element."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "adhō-kampa"@en .

aat:300446829 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lower fillet or lower kampa."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "adhaḥakampa"@en .

aat:300446830 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lower jaṅghā-register of a wall with two jaṅghās."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "talajaṅghā"@en .

aat:300446831 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lower profile of a Valabhī roof."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "skandha-vēdī"@en .

aat:300446833 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a lūmā with recessed courses."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "utkṣipta-lūmā"@en .

aat:300446834 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Mallets or blunt maces from the Indian subcontinent. Made either of wood or metal, having a spherical head mounted on a shaft, with a spike on the top. May be used as weapons, or as ceremonial objects that are highly decorated."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "gadās"@en .

aat:300446835 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a main ceiling of a hall with cusped and coffered courses (of kōlas and gajatālus)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sabhāmārga"@en .

aat:300446836 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a main enshrined deity."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mūlanāyaka"@en .

aat:300446837 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a main fronting dormer of a bhadraśālā."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "śālā-nāsī"@en .

aat:300446838 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a main temple."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mūlavimāna"@en .

aat:300446839 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a main temple as opposed to subsidiary shrines in a complex; main shrine; shrine proper."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "mūlaprāsāda"@en .

aat:300446841 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a major niche on the grīvā."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "grīvākōṣṭha"@en .

aat:300446842 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a major spire; minor spire."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "śikharikā"@en .

aat:300446843 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art and architecture, a makara head motif."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "makaramukha"@en .

aat:300446844 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a makara-bearing band in a base (in decorated Hoysaḷanāḍu temples)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "makarapīṭha"@en .

aat:300446845 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a makara-shaped gargoyle; makara-shaped water chute or conduit for discharging deity’s lustral water; elsewhere in halls, at eave-cornice, etc.; torana-arch spewed from the mouths of makaras, or formed from their tails."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "makara-praṇāla"@en .

aat:300446846 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a makara-snout projecting at temple-corners in gala and prastara."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "makaratuṇḍa"@en .

aat:300446847 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art and culture, one who adores or worships."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "ārādhaka"@en .

aat:300446848 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In India, demigods or nature spirits, often inoffensive tutelary guardians of a place, such as spirits of trees, mountains, streams, and forests."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "yakṣas"@en .

aat:300446849 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Representation of a male flywhisk-bearer figure as acolyte."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "cāmaradhara"@en .

aat:300446850 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art architecture, a male Jaina presiding deity."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "śāsanadēvatā"@en .

aat:300446851 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a mālikā; cloister."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "tirumāligai"@en .

aat:300446852 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, the cloister of a mālikā."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "āvṛtta-maṇḍapa"@en .

aat:300446853 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a mālikā-cloister; wall around the cuttambaiam."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "nālambalam"@en .

aat:300446854 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a maṇḍi-type."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "padmākāra"@en .

aat:300446855 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a maṇḍi-type made up of a circle of thickened petals simulating cobra-hoods."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "nāgadala"@en .

aat:300446856 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a maṇḍi-type made up of a circle of thickened petals simulating cobra-hoods."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "nāga-dalākṛti"@en .

aat:300446857 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a mansion pattern on gateway."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "tōraṇa-prāsāda"@en .

aat:300446858 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a bhavana is a temple, devotional place, or house of God. It is one of commonly used names for a temple, as found in Vāstuśāstra literature such the Mayamata and the Mānasāra."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "bhavanas"@en .

aat:300446859 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a manual of architecture; architectural tradition."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "vāstuśāstra"@en .

aat:300446860 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art and architecture, the measurement of the length of the body, including vertical measurements such as the distance fro mthe hair-limit to the eye-line, from that point to the tip of the nose, the length of the arms and of the legs and so on. These measurements constitute the six kinds of iconometric measurements as applied to standing, seated an reclining images."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "māna"@en .

aat:300446861 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a measuring cord."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "sūtra"@en .

aat:300446862 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a mesh, lattice, screen; perforated window."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "jālī"@en .

aat:300446863 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a middle band (wall-pilaster decoration); mediating decorative or plain band of a wall."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "madhyabandha"@en .

aat:300446864 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a middle band of a basal kumuda of the tripaṭṭa type; central band (on the kumuda)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "madhyapaṭṭa"@en .

aat:300446865 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a miniature bell, generally suspended from chain (decorative motif)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kiṅkiṇi"@en .

aat:300446866 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a miniature corner \"cogged wheel\" marking the symbolic storey in the vēṇukōśa of Kaliṅga temple śikhara; karṇāṇḍaka (Western India); corner \"cogged wheel\" marking the storey of a North Indian spire."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "bhūmi-āmalaka"@en .

aat:300446867 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a miniature curvilinear or pyramidal shrine-model placed over a pillaret; decorative motif arranged in vertical chains in the formation of Bhūmija superstructure."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kūṭastambha"@en .

aat:300446868 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a miniature cusped segment of ceiling; boar; decorative, semi-circular coffered ceiling course."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kōla"@en .

aat:300446869 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a vertical chain of decorative bālapañjara motifs positioned in the recesses between corner and flanking bands of a Latina superstructure."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "bālapañjara"@en .

aat:300446870 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a miniature kūṭa-shaped decorative motif; resembling square aedicula."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kūṭākāra"@en .

aat:300446871 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a miniature niche with nāsī-top."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "nāsikōṣṭha"@en .

aat:300446872 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a miniature simulacrum of a pillaret within a recessed moulding; vertical partition in the gala; vertical block at intervals inside the gala; gala block-projection."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "galapāda"@en .

aat:300446873 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a miniature square structure on corner of superstructure; corner aedicula, see kūṭa; kūṭa-turret placed above the karṇa-bay of a wall."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "karṇakūṭa"@en .

aat:300446874 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor angle."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kōṇikā"@en .

