    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor caitya-dormer; candraśālikā."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "ṭhakāra"@en .

aat:300446876 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor cyma moulding with lotus-petal pattern (in Dravidian architecture); minor padma moulding"@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kṣudrapadma"@en .

aat:300446877 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor cyma moulding; a minor inverted cyma recta."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "cippikā"@en .

aat:300446878 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor cyma-eave."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kapōtikā"@en .

aat:300446879 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian art and architecture, band showing ganders in file; minor decorative band showing haṁsas in formation."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "haṁsapaṭṭī"@en .

aat:300446880 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor dish-moulding over laśuna."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "tāṭi"@en .

aat:300446881 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor fillet."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kṣudra-vājana"@en .

aat:300446882 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor niche with Saṁvaraṇā roof; bell-topped miniature niche; a sort of Phāṁsa-kūṭa, carved (generally in series) on door-lintels, āsanapaṭṭa’s exterior face, etc."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "tilaka"@en .

aat:300446883 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor offset demarcating planes; minor facia in plan and elevation; chamfered subdivision or indentation in a ratha-buttress and in śikhara."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "phālanā"@en .

aat:300446884 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor offset flanking but sometimes forming part of the central offset; uparatha (Eastern India); anurāhā (Oriyā); minor side offsets of bhadra; minor side-offsets flanking the subhadra (central facet) of a bhadra."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "upabhadra"@en .

aat:300446885 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor projecting bracket (for supporting nāyikā or citraputrikā figure of a column in a hall)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "lumbikā"@en .

aat:300446886 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor roll-moulding."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "vṛttapaṭṭikā"@en .

aat:300446887 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor shrine(s) located at the corners of the temple; kōṇa-vimāna(s) subsidiary shrine placed at the corners of a pañcāyatana (5-shrined) complex; miniature temple situated at the corner of the main temple."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "karṇa-prāsādas"@en .

aat:300446888 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor sub-plinth course."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "kṣudrōpāna"@en .

aat:300446889 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor sub-plinth moulding."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "upānat"@en .

aat:300446890 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor vimāna on the bhadra axes of the main vimāna; may be attached or separated."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "bhadravimāna"@en .

aat:300446891 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Minor vimāna positioned along the diagonal axes of the vimāna."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "karṇavimāna"@en .

aat:300446892 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor/miniature eave-cornice, or rooflet."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "chādyakī"@en .

aat:300446893 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a minor/subsidiary shrine; peripheral shrine."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "dēvakulikā"@en .

aat:300446894 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, circular decorative mirror motif; usually in a pillar; medallion."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "darpaṇa"@en .

aat:300446895 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a mixed type; composite or polymorphic pillar-type, combining forms from square to polygonal to circular."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "miśra"@en .

aat:300446896 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a moat."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "parikhā"@en .

aat:300446897 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "In Indian architecture, a monastery."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:aat ;
    skos:prefLabel "muṭṭa"@en .

aat:300446899 a skos:Concept ;
