mimo:2382 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Bianschong"@zh,
        "Glacechord"@zh,
        "Glasharmonica"@zh,
        "Pienchong"@zh,
        "Pyeonjong"@zh,
        "cristallophone"@zh ;
    skos:definition "Bianzhong (Chinese:编钟) is an ancient Chinese musical instrument consisting of a set of bronze bells, played melodically. China is the earliest country to manufacture and use musical chimes. They are also called Chime Bells. These sets of chime bells were used as polyphonic musical instruments and some of these bells have been dated at between 2,000 to 3,600 years old. They were hung in a wooden frame and struck with a mallet. Using a wooden hammer and a rod to beat the bronze bell can make different pitch. Along with the stone chimes called bianqing, they were an important instrument in China's ritual and court music going back to ancient times."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bianzhong"@ca,
        "Bianzhong"@de,
        "Bianzhong"@en,
        "Bianzhong"@es,
        "Pien-chung"@fr,
        "Bianzhong"@it,
        "Bianzhong"@nl,
        "Bianzhong"@pl,
