        "Pienchong"@zh,
        "Pyeonjong"@zh ;
    skos:definition "A cowbell (or cow bell) is a bell worn around the neck of free-roaming livestock so herders can keep track of an animal via the sound of the bell when the animal is grazing out of view in hilly landscapes or vast plains. Although they are typically referred to as \"cow bells\" due to their extensive use with cattle, the bells are used on a wide variety of animals."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Esquella"@ca,
