mimo:2501 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Kou"@zh,
        "Pan-ku"@zh,
        "Silnyen"@zh,
        "Ting-shags"@zh,
        "Tingsha"@zh,
        "Xiaogu"@zh ;
    skos:definition "The bangu (Chinese: 板鼓; pinyin: bǎngǔ), often simply gu (Chinese: 鼓; pinyin: gǔ), is a Chinese frame drum that, when struck by one or two small bamboo sticks, creates a sharp dry sound essential to the aesthetics of Chinese opera. Striking the drum in different places produces different sounds. It is also used in many Chinese chamber music ensembles. The percussion section is very important in Chinese Opera, with battle or 'martial' scenes, which are called wu-chang. The bangu player is the director or conductor of the orchestra. He works with the other members of the percussion section to create the right mood for the audience and actors on stage."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bangu"@ca,
        "Bangu"@de,
        "Bangu"@en,
        "Bangu"@es,
        "Bangu"@fr,
        "Bangu"@it,
        "Bangu"@nl,
        "Bangu"@pl,
        "Bangu"@sv,
        "板鼓"@zh .

mimo:2504 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Tambour en tonneau"@fr,
        "Tambour en tonnelet"@fr,
        "Barrel shaped drum"@zh,
        "Tin-tin-sags"@zh ;
    skos:definition "Barrel drums are a class of membranophone, or drum, characterized by a barrel-shape with a bulge in the middle. They are often one-headed and open at the bottom. Examples include the Vietnamese trong chau and the bendre of the Mossi of Burkina Faso. Barrel drum is played horizontally."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tambor de barril"@ca,
        "Fasstrommel"@de,
        "Barrel drum"@en,
        "Tambor de barril"@es,
        "Tambour tonneau"@fr,
        "Tamburo a barile"@it,
        "Tontrom"@nl,
        "Bęben beczułkowaty"@pl,
        "Fattrumma"@sv,
        "桶鼓"@zh .

mimo:2506 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The bass drum is a large drum that produces a note of low definite or indefinite pitch. The instrument is typically cylindrical, with the drum's diameter much greater than the drum's depth, with a struck head at both ends of the cylinder. The heads may be made of calfskin or plastic and there is normally a means of adjusting the tension either by threaded taps or by strings. Bass drums are built in a variety of sizes, but size does not dictate the volume produced by the drum. The pitch and the sound can vary much with different sizes, but the size is also chosen based on convenience and aesthetics. Bass drums are percussion instruments and vary in size and are used in several musical genres. Three major types of bass drums can be distinguished."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tambor baix"@ca,
        "Basstrommel"@de,
        "Bass drum"@en,
        "Tambor bajo"@es,
        "Grosse caisse"@fr,
        "Grancassa"@it,
        "Grote trom"@nl,
        "Bęben basowy"@pl,
        "Bastrumma"@sv,
        "低音鼓"@zh .

