mimo:2703 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The pakhavaj is a barrel-shaped, two-headed drum, originating from the Indian subcontinent, the oldest version of double sided drums and its descendants are mridangam of Southern India and kendang of Maritime Southeast Asia and other South Asian double-headed drums. Its older forms were made with clay."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pakhavaj"@ca,
        "Pakhavaj"@de,
        "Pakhavaj"@en,
        "Pakhavaj"@es,
        "Pakhavaj"@fr,
        "Pakhavaj"@it,
        "Pakhavaj"@nl,
        "Pakhavaj"@pl,
        "Pakhavaj"@sv,
        "帕哈瓦雅鼓[印度]"@zh .

mimo:2704 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Nodo"@zh,
        "Pamba"@zh ;
    skos:definition "The pambai or pamba (Tamil: பம்பை) is a pair of cylindrical drums used in temple festivals and folk music in Tamil Nadu, India. There is a small community in southern Andhra who plays this instrument: the Pambalas. This unit of two drums is held near the waist of the player or put on the floor, and beaten with sticks, or with a hand and a stick. In the simpler varieties, both drums are made of wood, but there is a pambai in which one drum is of wood and the other of brass: the wooden one is known as veeru vanam and the metal drum as vengala pambai. The pambai is played in the traditional ensemble naiyandi melam."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pambai"@ca,
        "Pambai"@de,
        "Pambai"@en,
        "Pambai"@es,
        "Pambai"@fr,
        "Pambai"@it,
        "Pambai)"@nl,
        "Pambai"@pl,
        "Pambai"@sv,
        "帕姆巴鼓[印度]"@zh .

mimo:2706 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The pandeiro (Portuguese pronunciation: [pɐ̃ˈdejɾu]) is a type of hand frame drum popular in Brazil. The pandeiro is used in a number of Brazilian music forms, such as samba, choro, coco, and capoeira music."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pandeiro"@ca,
        "Pandeiro"@de,
        "Pandeiro"@en,
        "Pandeiro"@es,
        "Pandeiro"@fr,
        "Pandeiro"@it,
