mimo:2846 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Calembong"@zh,
        "Kye waing"@zh,
        "Kyee wain"@zh,
        "Talempoang"@zh ;
    skos:definition "Talempong is a traditional music of the Minangkabau people of Western Sumatra, Indonesia. The talempong produce a static texture consisting of interlocking rhythms. A talempong a small kettle gong which gives its name to an ensemble of four or five talempong as well as other gongs and drums. The term can refer to the instrument, the ensemble, or the genre of music. Talempong is in the form of a circle with a diameter of 15 to 17.5 centimeters, with a hollow hole at the bottom while at the top there is a roundabout with a diameter of five centimeters as a place to be hit. Talempong has a different tone. The sound is produced from a pair of wood hammered on its surface."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Talempong"@ca,
        "Talempong"@de,
        "Talempong"@en,
        "Talempong"@es,
