mimo:2884 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Damaha (Nepali: दमाहा) is a drum made from leather, brass or wood. It is played by striking with a stick. It is one of the instruments included in the Panche Baaja. The traditional players of this instrument are called Damai, a occupational caste who play different instrument in Nepali culture. The Damaha is bowl-shaped like a kettle drum and covered with animal hide. A neck strap is used to hold the damaha for the player while he plays."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Damaha"@ca,
        "Damaha"@de,
