mimo:2918 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The ilimba is a lamellophone from Tanzania. It is a traditional instrument of the Gogo ethnic group and its most famous player in the 20th century was Hukwe Zawose, who developed a version of the instrument with between 66 and 72 metal keys.[1] The instrument is similar to the Zimbabwean mbira but larger, and is tuned to intervals derived from the overtone series."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ilimba"@ca,
        "Ilimba"@de,
        "Ilimba"@en,
