mimo:2966 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A chime bar or resonator bell is a percussion instrument consisting of a tuned metal bar similar to a glockenspiel bar, with each bar mounted on its own wooden resonator. Chime bars are played with mallets again similar to a glockenspiel. The sound is similar to a glockenspiel, but with much more sustain, similar in this respect to a vibraphone but without the vibrato. * A single chime in G * The same chime disassembled to show the resonator and mounting"@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Barra de carillons"@ca,
        "Bar chime"@de,
        "Chime bar"@en,
        "Barra de carillones"@es,
        "Bar-chime"@fr,
        "Chime bar"@it,
        "Chime bar"@nl,
        "Dzwonki orkiestrowe"@pl,
        "Chime bar"@sv,
        "钟音条"@zh .

