mimo:2971 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A metallophone is any musical instrument in which the sound-producing body is a piece of metal (other than a metal string), consisting of tuned metal bars, tubes, rods, bowls, or plates. Most frequently the metal body is struck to produce sound, usually with a mallet, but may also be activated by friction, keyboard action, or other means."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Metal·lòfon"@ca,
        "Metallofon"@de,
        "Metallophone"@en,
        "Metalófono"@es,
