mimo:3441 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Ribab"@zh,
        "Saroda"@zh ;
    skos:definition "The sarod is a stringed instrument, used in Hindustani music on the Indian subcontinent. Along with the sitar, it is among the most popular and prominent instruments. It is known for a deep, weighty, introspective sound, in contrast with the sweet, overtone-rich texture of the sitar, with sympathetic strings that give it a resonant, reverberant quality. A fretless instrument, it can produce the continuous slides between notes known as meend (glissandi), which are important in Indian music."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sarod"@ca,
        "Sarod"@de,
        "Sarod"@en,
        "Sarod"@es,
