mimo:3460 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Surbahar (Hindi pronunciation: [s̪urbəhɑːr]; transl. Springtime of Notes) sometimes known as bass sitar, is a plucked string instrument used in the Hindustani classical music of the Indian subcontinent. It is closely related to the sitar, but has a lower pitch. Depending on the instrument's size, it is usually pitched two to five whole steps below the standard sitar."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Surbahar"@ca,
        "Sur-bahar"@de,
        "Surbahar"@en,
