        "Yue qin"@zh,
        "Yue-kin"@zh,
        "Yueh ch'in"@zh,
        "Yüa-tjin"@zh ;
    skos:definition "The yueqin (Chinese: 月琴; pinyin: Yuèqín; Japanese: 月琴, romanized: Gekkin; Korean: 월금/月琴, romanized: Wolgeum; Vietnamese: Nguyệt cầm), also called a moon lute or moon guitar, is a traditional Chinese string instrument. It is a lute with a round, hollow soundboard, a short fretted neck, and usually four strings. It is an important instrument in the Peking opera orchestra, often taking the role of main melodic instrument in lieu of the bowed string section."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Yueqin"@ca,
        "Yueqin"@de,
