mimo:3487 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Bàrbiton"@es,
        "Barbitos"@zh,
        "Dan doan"@zh ;
    skos:definition "The barbiton, or barbitos (Gr: βάρβιτον or βάρβιτος; Lat. barbitus), is an ancient stringed instrument related to the lyre known from Greek and Roman classics. The Greek instrument was a bass version of the kithara, and belonged in the zither family, but in medieval times, the same name was used to refer to the a different instrument that is a variety of lute."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bàrbiton"@ca,
