mimo:3522 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The a'dungu, also called the ekidongo or ennenga, is a stringed musical instrument of the Alur people of northwestern Uganda. It is an arched harp of varying dimensions, ranging from seven to ten strings or more. Tuning is not standardized, and players will usually tune by ear to each other shortly before a performance. The a'dungus are not in a particular key, and the tonality can be adapted to the preferences of the performers. Modern performers adept with the adungu include the native Ugandan musician James Makubuya and the American artist Crystal Bright."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Adungu"@ca,
        "Adungu"@de,
        "Adungu"@en,
        "Adungu"@es,
        "Adungu"@fr,
