mimo:3559 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A tenor violin (or tenor viola) is an instrument with a range between those of the cello and the viola. An earlier development of the evolution of the violin family of instruments, the instrument is not standard in the modern symphony orchestra. Its tuning, typically G2-D3-A3-E4 (an octave below the regular violin) places the range between the cello and viola and thus is sometimes confused with the modern baritone violin which has the same tuning on the standard violin body."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Violí tenor"@ca,
        "Bratsche"@de,
        "Tenor violin"@en,
        "Violín tenor"@es,
        "Ténor (violon)"@fr,
        "Violino tenore"@it,
        "Tenorviool"@nl,
        "Skrzypce tenorowe"@pl,
        "Tenorviolin"@sv,
        "次中音提琴"@zh .

