mimo:3568 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Elektrische Violine"@de,
        "Elektrogeige"@de ;
    skos:definition "An electric violin is a violin equipped with an electronic output of its sound. The term most properly refers to an instrument intentionally made to be electrified with built-in pickups, usually with a solid body. It can also refer to a violin fitted with an electric pickup of some type, although \"amplified violin\" or \"electro-acoustic violin\" are more accurate then."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
