mimo:3729 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "Zithers (/ˈzɪðər, ˈzɪθ-/; German: [ˈtsɪtɐ], from the Greek word cithara) are a class of stringed instruments. Historically, the name has been applied to any instrument of the psaltery family, or to an instrument consisting of many strings stretched across a thin, flat body. This article describes the latter variety."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Cítara"@ca,
