mimo:3845 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The launeddas (also called Sardinian triple clarinet) are a traditional Sardinian woodwind instrument made of three pipes, each of which has an single reed. They are a polyphonic instrument, with one of the pipes functioning as a drone and the other two playing the melody in thirds and sixths."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Launeddas"@ca,
        "Launedda"@de,
        "Launeddas"@en,
