mimo:3860 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The cornet (/ˈkɔːrnɪt/, US: /kɔːrˈnɛt/) is a brass instrument similar to the trumpet but distinguished from it by its conical bore, more compact shape, and mellower tone quality. The most common cornet is a transposing instrument in B♭, though there is also a soprano cornet in E♭ and cornets in A and C. All are unrelated to the Renaissance and early Baroque cornett."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Cornetí"@ca,
        "Kornett"@de,
        "Cornet"@en,
        "Cornetín"@es,
        "Cornet à pistons"@fr,
        "Cornetta"@it,
        "Cornet"@nl,
        "Kornet"@pl,
