mimo:3871 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The mute cornett was an important variant of the treble cornett and it was used in compositions by European composers in the 16th, 17th and 18th centuries. A significant number of mute cornetts have survived and are preserved in various European museums. Modern makers of cornetts produce mute cornetts and the numbers of recordings of music featuring this instrument has increased in recent years."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Corneta muda"@ca,
        "Stiller Zink"@de,
        "Mute cornett"@en,
        "Corneta muda"@es,
        "Cornet muet"@fr,
        "Cornetto muto"@it,
        "Stille zink"@nl,
        "Cynk prosty biały"@pl,
        "Sinkadus"@sv,
        "静音科尔内"@zh .

