        "Cornet droit"@fr,
        "Cornetto dritto"@it,
        "Rechte zink"@nl,
        "Cynk prosty"@pl,
        "Rak sinka"@sv,
        "直管科尔内"@zh .

mimo:3873 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The tenor cornett or lizard was a common musical instrument in the Renaissance and Baroque periods. This instrument was normally built in C and the pedal (lowest) note of the majority of tenor cornetts was the C below middle C. A number of surviving instruments feature a key to secure the lowest note. The instrument has a useful range of approximately two and a half octaves, however, an experienced player with a strong embouchure may be able to push the instrument higher."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Corneta tenor"@ca,
        "Tenorzink"@de,
        "Tenor cornett"@en,
        "Corneta tenor"@es,
