mimo:3940 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Flûte droite"@fr,
        "Flûte oblique"@fr,
        "Flûte à bouche terminale"@fr ;
    skos:definition "The end-blown flute (also called an edge-blown flute or rim-blown flute) is a woodwind instrument played by directing an airstream against the sharp edge of the upper end of a tube. Unlike a recorder or tin whistle, there is not a ducted flue voicing, also known as a fipple. Most rim-blown flutes are \"oblique\" flutes, being played at an angle to the body's vertical axis. A notched flute is an end-blown flute with a notch on the blowing surface. A lip-valley flute is a type of notched flute."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Flauta"@ca,
        "Längsflöte"@de,
        "End-blown flute"@en,
        "Flauta"@es,
        "Flûte à embouchure terminale"@fr,
        "Flauto a imboccatura apicale"@it,
        "Eindgeblazen fluit"@nl,
        "Flet o zadęciu krawędziowym"@pl,
        "Ändblåst flöjt"@sv,
        "竖吹长笛"@zh .

