        "Fluera"@zh,
        "Fouye"@zh,
        "Fuye"@zh ;
    skos:definition "Fue (笛/ふえ) is the Japanese word for bamboo flute, and refers to a class of flutes native to Japan. Fue come in many varieties, but are generally high-pitched and made of a bamboo called shinobue. The most popular of the fue is the shakuhachi."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Fue"@ca,
        "Fue"@de,
