    skos:altLabel "Chifte kavali"@zh,
        "Gaita embra y macho"@zh,
        "Gezi"@zh,
        "Kavali"@zh ;
    skos:definition "The kaval is a chromatic end-blown flute traditionally played throughout the Balkans (in Albania, Romania, Bulgaria, Southern Serbia, Kosovo, North Macedonia, Northern Greece, and elsewhere) and Anatolia (including Turkey and Armenia). The kaval is primarily associated with mountain shepherds."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
