    skos:altLabel "Svirjel"@de,
        "Chila chila"@zh,
        "Dentsivka"@zh,
        "Dudka"@zh,
        "Siaku-hachi"@zh ;
    skos:definition "Sopilka is a name applied to a variety of woodwind instruments of the flute family used by Ukrainian folk instrumentalists. Sopilka most commonly refers to a fife made of a variety of materials (but traditionally out of wood) and has six to ten finger holes. The term is also used to describe a related set of folk instruments similar to recorder, incorporating a fipple and having a constricted end."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sopilka"@ca,
        "Sopjelka"@de,
        "Sopilka"@en,
        "Sopilka"@es,
