mimo:4093 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A transverse flute or side-blown flute is a flute which is held horizontally when played. The player blows across the embouchure hole, in a direction perpendicular to the flute's body length. Transverse flutes include the Western concert flute, the Indian classical flutes (the bansuri and the venu), the Chinese dizi, the Western fife, a number of Japanese fue, and Korean flutes such as daegeum, junggeum and sogeum."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Flauta travessera"@ca,
        "Querflöte"@de,
        "Transverse flute"@en,
        "Flauta travesera"@es,
        "Flûte traversière"@fr,
        "Flauto traverso"@it,
        "Dwarsfluit"@nl,
        "Flet poprzeczny"@pl,
        "Traversflöjt"@sv,
        "Transverse flute"@zh .

