mimo:4144 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Ba wu"@zh,
        "Bawo"@zh,
        "Hsiuen"@zh,
        "T'ai-p'ing hsiao"@zh ;
    skos:definition "The bawu (simplified Chinese: 巴乌; traditional Chinese: 巴烏; pinyin: bāwū; also ba wu) is a Chinese wind instrument. Although shaped like a flute, it is actually a free reed instrument, with a single metal reed. It is played in a transverse (horizontal) manner. It has a pure, clarinet-like timbre and its playing technique incorporates the use of much ornamentation, particularly bending tones. This type of instrument is also used during Chinese New Years by the Taiwanese people next to mainland China."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bawu"@ca,
        "Bawu"@de,
        "Bawu"@en,
