mimo:4214 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The heckelphone (German: Heckelphon) is a musical instrument invented by Wilhelm Heckel and his sons. The idea to create the instrument was initiated by Richard Wagner, who suggested it at the occasion of a visit of Wilhelm Heckel in 1879. Introduced in 1904, it is similar to the oboe but, like the bass oboe, pitched an octave lower, the heckelphone having a significantly larger bore."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Heckelphone"@ca,
        "Heckelphon"@de,
        "Heckelphone"@en,
        "Heckelphone"@es,
        "Heckelphone"@fr,
