mimo:4325 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Bombardí, Eufoni"@ca ;
    skos:definition "The baritone horn, or sometimes just called baritone, is a low-pitched brass instrument in the saxhorn family. It is a piston-valve brass instrument with a bore that is mostly conical (like the higher pitched flugelhorn and alto (tenor) horn) but it has a narrower bore compared to the similarly pitched euphonium. It uses a wide-rimmed cup mouthpiece like that of its peers, the trombone and euphonium. Like the trombone and the euphonium, the baritone horn can be considered either a transposing or non-transposing instrument."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bugle baríton"@ca,
        "Bariton"@de,
        "Baritone bugle"@en,
        "Bugle barítono"@es,
