mimo:4390 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A cornu or cornum (Latin: cornū, cornūs or cornum, \"horn\", plural cornua, sometimes translated misleadingly as \"cornet\") was an ancient Roman brass instrument about 3 m (9.8 ft) long in the shape of a letter 'G'. The instrument was braced by a crossbar that stiffened the structure and provided a means of supporting its weight on the player's shoulder. Some specimens survive in the archaeological record, two from the ruins of Pompeii."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Cornu"@ca,
        "Cornu"@de,
        "Cornu"@en,
        "Cornu"@es,
