mimo:4402 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Dung kar"@zh,
        "Hai-lo"@zh,
        "Jinkai"@zh,
        "Rappakai"@zh ;
    skos:definition "Horagai (法螺貝) (or jinkai 陣貝) are large conch shells, usually from Charonia tritonis, that have been used as trumpets in Japan for many centuries. The instrument, which has served a number of purposes throughout Japanese history, has been given a number of Japanese names depending on its function. Special schools still teach students to play the traditional music associated with the conch."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Horagai"@ca,
        "Horagai"@de,
