mimo:4725 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The shvi (Armenian: շվի, \"whistle\", pronounced sh-vee) is an Armenian fipple flute with a labium mouth piece. Commonly made of wood (apricot, boxwood, or ebony) or bamboo and up to 12 inches (300 mm) in length, it typically has a range of an octave and a-half. The tav shvi is made from apricot wood, it is up to 18 inches (460 mm) long, and is tuned 1/4 lower producing a more lyrical and intimate sound."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Shvi"@ca,
        "Shvi"@de,
