mimo:4787 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The guitar zither (also chord zither, fretless zither, mandolin zither or harp zither) is a musical instrument consisting of a sound-box with two sets of unstopped strings. One set of strings is tuned to the diatonic, chromatic, or partially chromatic scale and the other set is tuned to make the various chords in the principal key of the melody strings. The name guitar zither is apparently derived from its sound. The mandolin zither (or mandolin harp) has doubled strings in unison courses producing a more mandolin-like sound."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Cítara-guitarra"@ca,
        "Gitarrenzither"@de,
        "Guitar-zither"@en,
        "Cítara-guitarra"@es,
        "Guitare-cithare"@fr,
        "Guitar-zither"@it,
        "Gitaarciter"@nl,
