mimo:4838 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Idiophone à friction"@fr ;
    skos:definition "Friction idiophones is designation 13 in the Hornbostel-Sachs system of musical instrument classification. These idiophones produce sound by being rubbed either against each other or by means of a non-sounding object. Instruments of this type are not very common; possibly the best known examples are the musical saw and the nail violin. According to Sachs,"@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Idiòfon de fricció"@ca,
