mimo:4932 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A dulcitone is a keyboard instrument in which sound is produced by a range of tuning forks, which vibrate when struck by felt-covered hammers activated by the keyboard.The instrument was designed by Thomas Machell of Glasgow in the 1860s, at the same time as Victor Mustel's organologically synonymous typophone, and manufactured by the firm of Thomas Machell & Sons during the late nineteenth and early twentieth centuries."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dulcitone"@ca,
