mimo:4961 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Windkapselschalmei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rauschpfeife is a commonly used term for a specific type of capped conical reed musical instrument of the woodwind family, used in Europe in the 16th and 17th centuries. In common with the crumhorn and cornamuse, it is a wooden double-reed instrument with the reed enclosed in a windcap. The player blows into a slot in the top of the windcap to produce the sound."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
