mimo:4969 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The terpodion or uranion is a keyboard instrument which produces sound using the same friction principle as the glass harmonica. Instead of rotating glass bells a wooden cylinder is rotating. This cylinder is coated with a special mixture. Only 25 instruments were ever built by Christian Friedrich Ludwig Buschmann, the son of Johann David Buschmann, the inventor of this instrument. Johann David Buschmann was first a passementier, then he started repairing key instruments. By 1817 the instrument spanned a range of 5 1/2 octaves."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Terpodion"@ca,
        "Terpodion"@de,
        "Terpodion"@en,
        "Terpodion"@es,
