mimo:5188 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "A dohol(Persian:دهل) is a large cylindrical drum with two skinheads. It is generally struck on one side with a wooden stick bowed at the end, and with a large thin stick on the other side, though it is also played with the bare hands. It is the principal accompaniment for the Sorna. A similar instrument, the Dhol, is used in traditional Egyptian, Pakistani and Indian music. The dohol is largely played in Kurdistan with the zurna."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dohol"@ca,
        "Dohol"@de,
        "Dohol"@en,
