mimo:5390 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The viola de cocho is a singular plucked string instrument from Brazil. It is typical in the states of Mato Grosso and Mato Grosso do Sul and has been designated a part of Brazil's intangible national heritage by IPHAN, the Brazilian institution responsible for the preservation of the national cultural heritage. It is unusual in that although it has only three frets at most and is left unvarnished. The Portuguese word cocho, used by farm labourers, refers to a hollowed-out log forming a sort of container. The cocho is widely used, for example, to provide salt for cattle on grassland farms."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Viola de cocho"@ca,
        "Viola de cocho"@de,
        "Viola de cocho"@en,
        "Viola de cocho"@es,
        "Viola de cocho"@fr,
        "Viola de cocho"@it,
        "Viola de cocho"@nl,
        "Viola de cocho"@pl,
        "Viola de cocho"@sv,
        "Viola de cocho"@zh .

