mimo:5410 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The taphon (Thai: ตะโพน, pronounced [ta.pʰoːn]) is a traditional drum of Thailand. It is barrel-shaped with two heads, and is played by the hands and fingers of both hands, much like the more popular congas. The taphon is very similar to the Cambodian sampho. An example of the taphon being played:"@en ;
