mimo:5759 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Kokiu"@zh,
        "Morin huur"@zh ;
    skos:definition "The morin khuur (Mongolian: морин хуур, romanized: morin khuur), also known as the horsehead fiddle, is a traditional Mongolian bowed stringed instrument. It is one of the most important musical instruments of the Mongol people, and is considered a symbol of the nation of Mongolia. The morin khuur is one of the Masterpieces of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Humanity identified by UNESCO."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Morin khuur"@ca,
