mimo:6524 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The qinqin (秦琴; pinyin: qínqín; Vietnamese: Đàn sến) is a plucked Chinese lute. It was originally manufactured with a wooden body, a slender fretted neck, and three strings.photo 1[ photo 2] Its body can be round,photo hexagonal (with rounded sides), or octagonal.[ photo] Often, only two strings were used, as in certain regional silk-and-bamboo ensembles.photo In its hexagonal form (with rounded sides), it is also referred to as meihuaqin (梅花琴, literally \"plum blossom instrument\")."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Qinqin"@ca,
        "Qinqin"@de,
        "Qinqin"@en,
        "Qinqin"@es,
