mimo:6642 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:definition "The Claviola is a musical instrument that was designed in the 1960s by Hohner technician and designer Ernst Zacharias (inventor of the Pianet and Clavinet). The instrument was produced for a few months in the late 1990s before being discontinued. Similar to a melodica (which is still in production), but worn like an accordion, the claviola has a set of piano keys on the right side that range 2½ octaves. The left side is a set of pipes that range in length depending on the corresponding pitch."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lev:mimo ;
    skos:prefLabel "Claviola"@ca,
        "Claviola"@de,
